@page "/products"

<PageTitle>Practice 2: Products</PageTitle>

<h1>Practice 2: Service-to-Result&lt;T&gt; Refactor</h1>
<p class="text-muted">
    The <code>ProductService</code> currently throws exceptions on validation failure.
    Refactor it to return <code>Result&lt;T&gt;</code> instead.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-info">
    <strong>Instructions:</strong>
    <ol class="mb-0 mt-2">
        <li>Open <code>Services/ProductService.cs</code> and <code>Services/IProductService.cs</code></li>
        <li>Change return types from <code>Task&lt;Product&gt;</code> to <code>Task&lt;Result&lt;Product&gt;&gt;</code></li>
        <li>Replace <code>throw</code> statements with <code>result.AddError()</code></li>
        <li>Return <code>result.WithValue()</code> on success</li>
        <li>In <code>AddAsync</code>, accumulate both name and price errors before returning</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5>Test Your Refactoring</h5>
        <p>After refactoring, the service methods should:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>GetByIdAsync(0)</code> -- returns Result with error "Product ID must be greater than zero"</li>
            <li><code>GetByIdAsync(99)</code> -- returns Result with error "Product with ID 99 not found"</li>
            <li><code>GetByIdAsync(1)</code> -- returns Result with Value = Wireless Mouse</li>
            <li><code>AddAsync(new Product(0, "", -5))</code> -- returns Result with TWO errors (name + price)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
